    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 test passing). The passing assertion `$.bulkSignupWarning == false` on the GET response confirms the field flows end-to-end.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `bulkSignupWarning` value depends on a *count of other owners* (created today), so it can't be a pure derived getter like `getLocality()`/`getMembershipTier()` \u2014 those have no repository access. It has to be captured at creation and persisted, exactly like `namesakeCount`. I followed that existing pattern:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning.java`. Reuses the existing `Registrations.countOn(...)` helper (the same accumulation path the daily-limit rule uses, per the test's own note) to count owners already registered on the new owner's registration date, and sets the flag to `count > 80`. Runs after `BuildOwner` (entity + rolled registration date exist) and before `SaveOwner` (so the new owner isn't counted).\n\n2. **Wired into** `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` as `assignBulkSignupWarning`, between `assignNamesakeCount` and `assignCustomerCode`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `bulk_signup_warning` boolean column with `isBulkSignupWarning()`/`setBulkSignupWarning()`.\n\n4. **OpenAPI schema** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and MapStruct maps it automatically (no mapper change needed).\n\n5. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE` to all four `schema.sql` files (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres). The `NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE` keeps seed rows (whose inserts list columns explicitly) and any legacy rows at `false`, matching the \"otherwise false\" requirement.\n\nEach piece sits in its single-responsibility unit and reuses existing helpers rather than duplicating the counting logic.",
